# 2. Previous Release Branch Display (Production Kubernetes)

Current behavior:

Previous branch is fetched correctly from Production Kubernetes.

Example value coming from Kubernetes:

```
release-26-07-rel
```

Actual Git branch:

```
release/26.07.rel
```

The Kubernetes value is correct internally.

However the UI is displaying that value directly.

Users think this branch never exists.

## Required behavior

When displaying Previous Branch:

- Preserve the original production value internally.
- Maintain Production Branch Name exactly as received.
- While showing Previous Branch in UI:

Find the matching Git branch from the GitHub branch list.

Display:

```
release/26.07.rel
```

instead of

```
release-26-07-rel
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- Internal Production branch remains unchanged.
- Previous Branch displayed must always exist in GitHub.
- User must never see invalid/non-existing branch names.
- Existing production resolution logic must remain unchanged.
- Resolution Source logic must remain unchanged.

